@flexiarg operator/show-a-memory-bears-on-the-reply
@title A Memory Indicator Must Show That The Memory Changed What The Agent Said
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-blG3JA turn-scGeaB
@parent memory/name-a-reusable-artifact
@context A demo marks memories as in-force and shows indicators, but the agent's replies show no change.

! conclusion: show, per turn, which memory shaped which part of the reply, and over time how it develops

  + IF:
    patterns or memories are said to be active

  + HOWEVER:
    the display cannot tell active from used, so Joe cannot see any effect

  + THEN:
    show, per turn, which memory shaped which part of the reply, and over time how it develops

  + BECAUSE:
    only a memory that witnesses its own use can be shown to matter
